  "id": "methadone-maintenance-therapy",
  "term": "methadone maintenance therapy",
  "definition": "Methadone maintenance therapy is a harm-reduction program for people who inject drugs that uses methadone and is intended to help prevent and control HIV and other blood-borne infections linked to needle sharing. In the source, people enrolled in this program are described as a high-risk group for hepatitis C and as having reduced injecting behavior.",
